---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { SITE } from "../site.config.js";
import { breadcrumbSchema } from "../lib/schema.js";

const crumbs = [{ name: "Terms of Use", path: "/terms/" }];
const schema = [breadcrumbSchema(crumbs)];
---

<Base
  title="Terms of Use"
  description={`Terms of use for ${SITE.name}: permitted use, not legal or tax advice, accuracy and updates, advertising and limitation of liability.`}
  schema={schema}
  crumbs={crumbs}
>
  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-12 lg:py-16">
    <div class="bg-white rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 p-8 sm:p-12 shadow-sm prose prose-slate max-w-none text-sm text-slate-700 leading-relaxed">
      <h1 class="text-3xl font-extrabold text-slate-900 not-prose">Terms of Use</h1>
      <p class="text-xs text-slate-500">Last Revised: November 2026</p>

      <hr class="my-6" />

      <h2>1. Acceptance of these terms</h2>
      <p>
        By using {SITE.name}, you agree to these Terms of Use. If you do not agree, please do not use the calculators or articles.
      </p>

      <h2>2. What the site is for</h2>
      <p>
        The calculators and articles are provided for personal, educational, and informational use. You may use them to compare job offers, check paycheck figures, or plan a household budget.
      </p>

      <h2>3. Not legal, tax, or financial advice</h2>
      <p>
        {SITE.name} publishes general information about wages, overtime, and payroll taxes. It is not legal, tax, accounting, or financial advice, and reading it does not create a professional relationship with the author. Wage and tax rules depend on your state, your employer, and your situation. For a decision that matters, check the primary source linked in the article and ask a qualified professional or your state labor agency.
      </p>

      <h2>4. Accuracy and updates</h2>
      <p>
        We cite primary sources and recompute examples, but tax brackets, wage bases, and minimum wages change often, and errors can happen. Where an article uses a figure from a particular year, it says so. If you find an error, tell us at <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a> and verified errors are corrected.
      </p>

      <h2>5. Intellectual property</h2>
      <p>
        The text, tables, and design of this site belong to {SITE.name} unless stated otherwise. You may quote short excerpts with a link back to the source page. Please do not copy whole articles or republish them without permission. Legal texts, regulations, and agency publications cited here belong to their original publishers.
      </p>

      <h2>6. Third-party links and advertising</h2>
      <p>
        Articles link to government and other external sites that we do not control. The site may show advertising; advertisers do not review or influence our articles, and an ad is not an endorsement. See the <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a> for how advertising cookies work.
      </p>

      <h2>7. Limitation of liability</h2>
      <p>
        The calculators and articles are provided as is, without warranties of any kind. To the extent allowed by law, {SITE.name} and its author are not liable for losses that result from relying on the site. Check results against your actual pay records and official sources before you act on them.
      </p>

      <h2>8. Changes</h2>
      <p>
        We may update these terms. The date at the top shows the latest revision. Continuing to use the site after a change means you accept the updated terms.
      </p>

      <h2>9. Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about these terms: <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
